  "usage_note": "**Everybody** and **everyone** mean the same thing and can normally replace each other; **everybody** is slightly more conversational. Both take a singular verb, though a plural pronoun (**they**, **their**) is now the usual way to refer back to them when the person's sex is not known: *everybody brought their own lunch*.",
